  discoveredBy: William Ramsay
  description: "Krypton (from Greek:\u03BA\u03C1\u03C5\u03C0\u03C4\u03CC\u03C2 kryptos
    \"the hidden one\") is a chemical element with symbol Kr and atomic number 36.
    It is a member of group 18 (noble gases) elements. A colorless, odorless, tasteless
    noble gas, krypton occurs in trace amounts in the atmosphere, is isolated by
    fractionally distilling liquefied air, and is often used with other rare gases
    in fluorescent lamps."
